# 38. Understand `/etc/sudoers`

View safely:

```bash
sudo cat /etc/sudoers
```

**Do not edit `/etc/sudoers` directly with nano/vim.**

Use:

```bash
sudo visudo
```

Why?

`visudo` checks syntax before saving and helps prevent locking administrators out of sudo because of a syntax mistake.

---

# 39. Create a Dedicated Sudoers File

Best practice is usually to put custom rules in:

```text
/etc/sudoers.d/
```

Create:

```bash
sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/linux-admin
```

For example:

```text
developer1 ALL=(ALL) /usr/bin/systemctl status nginx
```

This would allow `developer1` to run only that specific command through sudo.

Test:

```bash
sudo -l -U developer1
```

