# 40. Least Privilege Exercise

Create a support user:

```bash
sudo useradd -m support1
sudo passwd support1
```

We want:

```text
support1
   |
   +---- Can check nginx status
   |
   +---- Cannot stop nginx
   |
   +---- Cannot become root
```

Create:

```bash
sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/support1
```

Add:

```text
support1 ALL=(root) /usr/bin/systemctl status nginx
```

Then:

```bash
sudo -l -U support1
```

This is a very good **Linux Administrator interview scenario**.

