## 🔥 Administrator rule to remember

When a user says:

> **"I can't access something."**

Don't immediately run `chmod 777`.

Investigate:

```text
             User
               ↓
          id username
               ↓
          Group membership
               ↓
       File ownership
               ↓
        File permissions
               ↓
             ACL
               ↓
           SELinux
               ↓
          Application
```

**Never use `chmod 777` as your first troubleshooting solution.** That's a common bad practice and an interview red flag.

